I would like to add another point that has been brought up by many users. The story is full of inconsistencies. It's not uncommon to find a character being killed by a gunshot that was not even fired. This is an important point. I have seen this happen in several other stories. In addition to the "fire" the characters were shot, there were also shots fired at them by the other characters. These were not gunshots, but people being shot. As a reader, I really don't want to read that and then have the character I loved get shot by someone else. Therefore, the inconsistencies in the shooting are a major reason for me to skip this story. If it was a story about a military mission I would be very interested in it, because it is a very interesting premise. However, this is not a war story, it's a police story and I am not interested. So, if you are looking for a great story to start your weekend with, maybe give this one a try. But, for now, don’t give me any more reason to leave you. Thanks for reading. :)
